OL,3,AMiliband says slavery apology will not
OL,4,Abring cost for UK taxpayers
OL,5,
OL,6,FSpeaking on the BBC's Newscast podcast,
OL,7,FMiliband said previous British
OL,8,Fgovernments had a "sweep it under the
OL,9,Fcarpet" attitude to the pain and
OL,10,Fconsequences of slavery, citing what he
OL,11,Fdescribed as former Prime Minister Sir
OL,12,FTony Blair's "sorry not sorry" remarks
OL,13,Fon the issue nearly two decades ago.
OL,15,FIn 2007, Sir Tony said the UK's
OL,16,Finvolvement in the slave trade was a
OL,17,Fmatter of "deep sorrow and regret".
OL,23,APub: 04-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG8/39
